3/3/71-AIS (IV), dated 22nd July, 1971]
:
Provided that for purposes of selection under sub-rule (1) read with sub-rule (3-A) of rule 4 of the Indian Forest Service
(Recruitment) Rules, 1966, to the Cadre for the State of Punjab as it existed immediately before the 1st November,
1966, that is to say, before the Reorganization of that State under the Punjab Reorganization Act, 1966 (
31 of 1966
), the Special Selection Board shall consist of the following :
(i)
the Chairman of the Commission or his nominee;
(ii)
the Inspector General of Forests of the Government of India or such other officer as may be nominated by the Central
Government in this behalf;
(iii)
an officer of the Government of India not below the rank of Joint Secretary;
(iv)
the Chief Secretary to the Government of Punjab or a Secretary to that State Government nominated by him;
(v)
the Secretary to the Government of Punjab dealing with Forests or the Chief Conservator of Forests, Punjab;
(vi)
the Chief Secretary to the Government of Haryana or a Secretary to that State Government nominated by him;
(vii)
